IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain

-- g1-register.l4: s.11 of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or Air-Conditioning Systems Law
-- 5785-2025 (Sefer HaChukim 3349 p. 185), the register of licensees.  Group G1.
-- Imports prelude, daydate and domain.  The Hebrew is copied by script from inputs/law.wiki (src:N is line N);
-- identifiers and glosses are mine and the Hebrew governs.
--
-- The register's contents are projections of the domain Licence record, which is "a licence as the register of s.11
-- records it".  The domain Person carries only a reference and a kind: the holder's other "details" (name, address)
-- are a nouns request in FRAGMENT-G1.md, so `the details of the licensee` is a Person here.

§ `Chapter 2: Licensing (continued)`

§§ `s.11 Register of licensees`

@desc The acts of section 11: the Registrar keeps the register, and (on one reading) opens it to public inspection by query
DECLARE `Act under section 11` IS ONE OF
    `keep a register of licensees`
    `open the register to public inspection by query`

-- s.11(a): the Registrar shall keep a register of licensees that includes (1) the licensee's details, the kind of
-- licence he holds and its validity period, and (2) the revocation or suspension of a licence.  No period is stated.
-- src:122 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} הרשם ינהל מרשם של בעלי רישיונות שיכלול פרטים אלה:
-- src:123 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} פרטי בעל הרישיון, סוג הרישיון שבידו ותקופת תוקפו;
-- src:124 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} ביטול או התליה של רישיון.
@ref s.11(a) (src:122-124)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under section 11`
`s 11(a) — the Registrar must keep a register of licensees` MEANS
    PARTY `the Registrar`
    MUST `keep a register of licensees`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Registrar`
          BECAUSE "section 11(a): the Registrar did not keep a register of licensees with the details the section lists"

@ref s.11(a)(1) (src:123); s.11(a)(2) (src:124)
@desc One entry of the register of licensees: what section 11(a) says the register includes about one licence
DECLARE `Entry of the register of licensees` HAS
    `the details of the licensee` IS A Person @desc The person who holds the licence
    `the kind of licence` IS A `Licence kind` @desc The kind of licence the licensee holds
    `the licence was granted on` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the validity period
    `the licence is valid until` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The last day of the validity period the register shows; NOTHING if no end is recorded
    `revoked on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day the licence was revoked under section 10; NOTHING if it was not
    `suspended from` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The first day of a suspension under section 10; NOTHING if it was never suspended
    `suspended until` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The last day of a suspension; NOTHING if there is no end fixed or no suspension

-- The entry the register holds for a licence: the holder, the kind, the validity period (s.11(a)(1)); the
-- revocation or suspension (s.11(a)(2)).
@ref s.11(a)(1) (src:123); s.11(a)(2) (src:124)
@export The register entry for a licence: the holder's details, the kind of licence, the validity period, and any revocation or suspension (section 11(a))
GIVEN licence IS A Licence @desc The licence as the register records it
GIVETH AN `Entry of the register of licensees`
`s 11(a) — the register entry for the licence` licence MEANS
    `Entry of the register of licensees` WITH
        `the details of the licensee` IS licence's `the holder`
        `the kind of licence` IS licence's `the kind of licence`
        `the licence was granted on` IS licence's `granted on`
        `the licence is valid until` IS licence's `validity ends on, as recorded`
        `revoked on` IS licence's `revoked on`
        `suspended from` IS licence's `suspended from`
        `suspended until` IS licence's `suspended until`

-- Whether the entry shows the validity period (s.11(a)(1)): a licence with no end of validity recorded has no
-- validity period to show.
@ref s.11(a)(1) (src:123)
GIVEN entry IS AN `Entry of the register of licensees`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(a)(1) — the entry shows the validity period` entry MEANS
    CONSIDER entry's `the licence is valid until`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST end THEN end AT LEAST entry's `the licence was granted on`

@ref s.11(a)(2) (src:124)
GIVEN entry IS AN `Entry of the register of licensees`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(a)(2) — the entry shows a revocation` entry MEANS
    CONSIDER entry's `revoked on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST day THEN TRUE

@ref s.11(a)(2) (src:124)
GIVEN entry IS AN `Entry of the register of licensees`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(a)(2) — the entry shows a suspension` entry MEANS
    CONSIDER entry's `suspended from`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST day THEN TRUE

-- s.11(b): "The register shall be open to public inspection by way of a query in which identifying details of the
-- person about whom the information is sought are stated."  A passive sentence with no actor: a constitutive rule about
-- what inspection the register is open to, not a duty on the Registrar (the Law writes none).  A query that states no
-- identifying details is not one the register is open to: the answer names the problem.  A person is identified by the
-- reference of the domain Person.
-- src:125 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} המרשם יהיה פתוח לעיון הציבור בדרך של שאילתה שבה יצוינו פרטים מזהים של האדם שלגביו מתבקש המידע.
@ref s.11(b) (src:125)
@desc A query of the register of licensees: the details of the person asked about
DECLARE `Query of the register of licensees` HAS
    `identifying details of the person asked about were stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the query states identifying details of the person about whom the information is sought
    `the reference for the person asked about` IS A STRING @desc The reference (national or company number or the like) that identifies the person asked about; the empty string if none is stated

@desc Why a query of the register of licensees cannot be answered
DECLARE `Problem with a query of the register of licensees` IS ONE OF
    `the query states no identifying details of the person asked about`

@ref s.11(b) (src:125)
@export What the register shows a member of the public who queries it with identifying details of a person: every entry for the licences that person holds or held; a query that states no identifying details is not one the register is open to
GIVEN query IS A `Query of the register of licensees` @desc The query: the identifying details of the person asked about
      register IS A LIST OF `Entry of the register of licensees` @desc Every entry of the register
GIVETH AN EITHER `Problem with a query of the register of licensees` (LIST OF `Entry of the register of licensees`)
`s 11(b) — the register shows, on a query` query register MEANS
    IF       query's `identifying details of the person asked about were stated`
         AND NOT (query's `the reference for the person asked about` EQUALS "")
    THEN RIGHT (filter (GIVEN entry YIELD (entry's `the details of the licensee`)'s `reference for the person` EQUALS (query's `the reference for the person asked about`)) register)
    ELSE LEFT `the query states no identifying details of the person asked about`

-- The same passive sentence read as a duty: "the register shall be open" implies that the Registrar, who keeps it, must
-- open it.  The Law writes no such duty and names no actor (a passive sentence is not a duty, entry 5.2 of the phrasebook);
-- the reading is callable here.  No period is stated.
@ref s.11(b) (src:125)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under section 11`
`s 11(b) — the Registrar must open the register to public inspection by query, on the reading that the passive sentence implies a duty` MEANS
    PARTY `the Registrar`
    MUST `open the register to public inspection by query`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Registrar`
          BECAUSE "section 11(b): the Registrar did not open the register to public inspection by a query that states identifying details of the person"
